Z||000000||Pyric||12-18-2001||07:16 PM||||Well, I've fixed my problem with the manifold glowing and the car wont stay idling.  it starts fine.  After turning the key it jumps up to 3500 rpms and then drops to idle speed of about 1000- 1500 rpms.  Then it drops below 1000 and the engine stalls.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>If I give it gas before it stalls for about 30 seconds then it will drop to 1000 and idle fine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>I'm lost on this one.<P>I've replaced:<BR>the vacuum lines<BR>EGR tube<BR>EGR valve<BR>coolant temp sensor<BR>cold start sensor,<BR>vapor canister <BR>Throttle position sensor<BR>sparkplugs<BR>ECM and Prom<BR>thermostat<BR>and <BR>I was told by the previous owner that he had just replaced:<BR>the Idle Air control<BR>Distributor<BR>pickup coil<P>Oh, and it's a brand new engine with only 12 miles on it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Any ideas?<P>I don't understand how after warming up it can idle at 1000rpms fine, but when cold it stalls at the same rpm.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieronegS.jpg">   <P><BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||12-18-2001||07:49 PM||||the Idle Air control has a plug clip for wires pull off and spray clean with WD-40<BR>on both sides. cheap if it works and has worked for me.<BR>or check cold start jet and wires to it.<BR>throtal plate too far open at start?<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
