Z||000004||Rodrv6||12-19-2001||05:42 PM||||Have you driven it for a while?  The car needs to be driven over 40 MPH with the engine fully warmed up in order for the ECM to reset itself.  Also, the ECM will "learn" the engine settings over a period of time while you drive the car.  You may want to double check the timing--the V6 seems to be very sensitive to too much advance (at least mine is).<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
